18:["$","$L1f",null,{"data":{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Who are the online Quran tutors at QuranCrest Academy?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"QuranCrest's current teaching faculty includes Maulana Muhammad Bakhtiar, Maulana Qazi Amjad and Alimah Sumera. Their published profiles explain their education, experience and teaching areas without making unverified certification claims."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I choose a male or female Quran teacher?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Families and adult learners can share a male or female tutor preference during the free assessment. Final matching depends on the course, learner's level, language, time zone and current tutor availability."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How does QuranCrest match a tutor with a learner?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The coordinator first considers the learner's age, present reading level, chosen course, preferred language, tutor preference and suitable local times. The aim is to arrange a practical teaching match rather than assign the same pathway to every student."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can parents remain aware of a child's online lessons?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Parents or guardians should manage enrollment, know the class schedule and remain reasonably available for younger learners. QuranCrest recommends that children attend from a shared or observable area of the home."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why is the female teacher's face not shown?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Her profile image is intentionally privacy-protected. The visual is a representative illustration rather than a personal photograph, and this is stated clearly so families are not misled."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I discuss the tutor before regular classes begin?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Use the free assessment to discuss the learner's goals, course, preferred tutor, language and schedule before deciding on a regular lesson plan."}}]}}]
